<h2 id="gmtool-license">gmtool license</h2>
<p><img alt="License badge" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-paid-blue"></p>
<p>The <code>license</code> command group allows you to perform actions related to the Genymotion&nbsp;license. Commands available within this group are:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>info</code>: Returns the license type, number of activated workstations and expiration date.</li>
<li><code>register &lt;license_key&gt;</code>: Registers a license key or renews Genymotion Desktop&nbsp;activation.</li>
<li><code>count</code>: Returns the number of activated workstations with the registered license key.</li>
<li><code>validity</code>: Returns the number of days of validity remaining for the registered license key.</li>
</ul>
<div class="admonition example">
<p class="admonition-title">Example</p>
<p></p><div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_6"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_6 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>gmtool<span class="w"> </span>license<span class="w"> </span>register<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">0123456789</span>
</code></pre></div>
Registers the license key <code>0123456789</code> and authenticates the user with the email and password provided by the <a href="https://docs.genymotion.com/tools/desktop/gmtool/#gmtool-config">config</a> command.<p></p>
</div>
<h2 id="gmtool-config">gmtool config</h2>
<p><img alt="License badge" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-paid-blue"></p>
<p>The <code>config</code> command group allows you to define Genymotion Desktop&nbsp;settings. Options available within this group are:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>--email &lt;email&gt;</code>: Account Email.</li>
<li><code>--password &lt;password&gt;</code>: Account Password.</li>
<li><code>--license_server &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Use a company license server instead of Genymobile ones to activate your copy of Genymotion. Default is <strong>off</strong>.</li>
<li><code>--license_server_address &lt;url&gt;</code>: Url of the license server.</li>
<li><code>--statistics &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Allows statistics to be send anonymously.</li>
<li><code>--virtual_device_path &lt;path&gt;</code>: Path to where the devices are deployed.</li>
<li><code>--use_custom_sdk &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Enable or disable the use of a specified Android SDK.</li>
<li><code>--sdk_path &lt;path&gt;</code>: Path to the Android SDK.</li>
<li><code>--screen_capture_path &lt;path&gt;</code>: Screen capture destination folder.</li>
<li><code>--proxy &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Enable or disable the use of a proxy.</li>
<li><code>--proxy_type &lt;http/socks5&gt;</code>: Type of proxy : http or socks5.</li>
<li><code>--proxy_address &lt;url&gt;</code>: Proxy URL.</li>
<li><code>--proxy_port &lt;port&gt;</code>: Proxy port.</li>
<li><code>--proxy_auth &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Enable or disable proxy authentication.</li>
<li><code>--proxy_username &lt;username&gt;</code>: Proxy authentication username.</li>
<li><code>--proxy_password &lt;password&gt;</code>: Proxy authentication password.</li>
<li><code>--trusted_hosts &lt;host, ...&gt;</code>: Trusted hosts for which SSL errors will be ignored.</li>
<li><code>--shared_clipboard &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Enable or disable shared clipboard.</li>
<li><code>--hypervisor &lt;virtualbox/qemu&gt;</code>: Select which hypervisor to use: virtualbox or qemu.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="gmtool-admin">gmtool admin</h2>
<p>The <code>admin</code> command group allows you to administrate virtual devices.</p>
<h3 id="basic-commands">Basic commands</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>start &lt;device&gt;</code>: Starts the specified virtual device. Add the <code>--coldboot</code> option to force a complete boot cycle.</li>
<li><code>stop &lt;device&gt;</code>: Stops the specified virtual device.</li>
<li><code>list</code>: Lists all virtual devices. Available filter options are:<ul>
<li><code>--running</code>: lists running virtual devices only.</li>
<li><code>--off</code>: lists stopped virtual devices only.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<div class="admonition example">
<p class="admonition-title">Example</p>
<p>Start the virtual device named "My Phone":</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_7"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_7 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>gmtool<span class="w"> </span>admin<span class="w"> </span>start<span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"My Phone"</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>List all the running virtual devices:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_8"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_8 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>gmtool<span class="w"> </span>admin<span class="w"> </span>list<span class="w"> </span>--running
</code></pre></div>
</div>
<h3 id="advanced-commands">Advanced commands</h3>
<p><img alt="License badge" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-paid-blue"></p>
<ul>
<li><code>details &lt;device&gt;</code>: Returns the properties of one or more specified virtual devices. If no virtual device is specified, returns the properties of all virtual devices.</li>
<li><code>stopall</code>: Stops all virtual devices.</li>
<li><code>factoryreset &lt;device&gt;</code>: Restores the specified virtual device to factory state.</li>
<li><code>delete &lt;device&gt;</code>: Deletes the specified virtual device.</li>
<li><code>clone &lt;source&gt; &lt;target&gt;</code>: Duplicates the specified virtual device (source) to a new virtual device (target).</li>
<li>
<p><code>templates</code><sup><span class="twemoji"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 3v1H4v2h1v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6h1V4h-5V3zm0 5h2v9H9zm4 0h2v9h-2z"></path></svg></span></sup>: Lists all online and offline available virtual device templates and their basic properties.</p>
<div class="admonition warning">
<p class="admonition-title">This command is deprecated. Please use <code>hwprofiles</code> and <code>osimages</code> commands instead.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>hwprofiles</code>: List all available hardware profiles.</p>
</li>
<li><code>osimages</code>: List all available Android images.</li>
<li><code>logzip &lt;path&gt;</code>: Generates an archive of all Genymotion Desktop&nbsp;log files. Specify <code>path</code> to generate the logs in a specific path. Add option <code>-n/--name &lt;device&gt; &lt;path&gt;</code> to generate a log archive of the specified virtual device, at the defined location. If an archive file already exists, it will be overwritten.</li>
<li><code>create &lt;hwprofile&gt; &lt;osimage&gt; &lt;device&gt;</code>: Creates a virtual device from the specified hardware profile (<code>hwprofile</code>) and Android OS version (<code>osimage</code>). Available options are:<ul>
<li><code>--density &lt;value&gt;</code>: Sets the screen density of the virtual device in pixels per inch. Available densities are: 120, 160, 213, 240, 260, 280, 300, 320, 340, 360, 400, 420, 440, 450, 480, 560 and 640.</li>
<li><code>--width &lt;value&gt;</code>: Sets the screen width of the virtual device.
-<code>--height &lt;value&gt;</code>: Sets the screen height of the virtual device.</li>
<li><code>--virtualkeyboard &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Activates or deactivates the virtual keyboard.</li>
<li><code>--navbar &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Displays or hides the Android&nbsp;navigation bar in the virtual device.</li>
<li><code>--nbcpu &lt;value&gt;</code>: Sets the number of processors used by the virtual device.</li>
<li><code>--ram &lt;value&gt;</code>: Sets the memory space allocated to the virtual device in MB.</li>
<li><code>--network-mode &lt;nat/bridge&gt;</code>: Sets the host network interface mode for the virtual device. <strong>Only available with VirtualBox hypervisor.</strong></li>
<li><code>--bridged-if &lt;interface_name&gt;</code>: When network mode is bridge, sets the bridged interface for the virtual device. <strong>Only available with VirtualBox hypervisor.</strong></li>
<li><code>--sysprop &lt;property&gt;:&lt;value&gt;</code>: Sets a build system property of the virtual device. Available properties are: <code>MODEL</code>, <code>PRODUCT</code>, <code>MANUFACTURER</code>,<code>BOARD</code>, <code>BRAND</code>, <code>DEVICE</code>, <code>DISPLAY</code>, <code>SERIAL</code>, <code>TYPE</code>, <code>FINGERPRINT</code> and <code>TAGS</code>. Values for each property are detailed at <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Build.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">developer.android.com<sup><span class="twemoji"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 3v2h3.59l-9.83 9.83 1.41 1.41L19 6.41V10h2V3m-2 16H5V5h7V3H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-7h-2z"></path></svg></span></sup></a>.</li>
<li><code>--quickboot &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Set default for the use of a resume state. <strong>Only available with QEMU hypervisor!</strong></li>
<li><code>--root-access &lt;on/off&gt;</code>: Set root access. <strong>Only applies to non-rooted Android versions</strong></li>
<li><code>edit &lt;device&gt;</code>: Edits the specified virtual device settings. See <code>create</code> subcommand for detailed options and values.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<div class="admonition example">
<p class="admonition-title">Examples</p>
<p>Create a device named "My Samsung Phone" with the <em>Samsung Galaxy S10</em> profile, Android 11.0 and default settings:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_9"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_9 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>gmtool<span class="w"> </span>admin<span class="w"> </span>create<span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"Samsung Galaxy S10"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"Android 11.0"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"My Samsung Phone"</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>Create a device named "My Custom Phone" with the <em>Custom Phone</em> profile, Android 11.0, 1440x2560 display resolution, 560dpi, 4 CPUs and 4GB in RAM:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_10"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_10 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>gmtool<span class="w"> </span>admin<span class="w"> </span>create<span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"Custom Phone"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"Android 11.0"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"My Custom Phone"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="se">\</span>
--width<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">1440</span><span class="w"> </span>--height<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">2560</span><span class="w"> </span>--density<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">560</span><span class="w"> </span>--nbcpu<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">4</span><span class="w"> </span>--ram<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">4096</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>Change the "My Custom Phone" device display resolution to 728x1024 and 240dpi (hdpi):</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_11"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_11 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>gmtool<span class="w"> </span>admin<span class="w"> </span>edit<span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"My Custom Phone"</span><span class="w"> </span>--width<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">728</span><span class="w"> </span>--height<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">1024</span><span class="w"> </span>--density<span class="w"> </span>hdpi
</code></pre></div>
</div>
<h2 id="gmtool-device">gmtool device</h2>
<p><img alt="License badge" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-paid-blue"></p>
<p>The <code>device</code> command group allows you to directly interact with a virtual device.</p>
<p>Options available for each subcommands within this group are:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>-n/--name &lt;device&gt;</code>: Interacts with the specified virtual device. If not specified, interacts with the running virtual device. <strong>If more than one virtual device is running, the use of options <code>-n</code> or <code>--all</code> is mandatory.</strong></li>
<li><code>--all</code>: Interacts with all running virtual devices.</li>
<li><code>--start</code>: Starts the virtual device specified by <code>-n</code> if not already started.</li>
</ul>
<p>Commands available in the <code>device</code> command group are:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>logcatdump &lt;file&gt;</code>: Copies the logcat output onto the specified destination file. If a logcat dump file already exists, it will be overwritten.</li>
<li><code>logcatclear</code>: Empties the logcat content of a virtual device.</li>
<li><code>push &lt;source&gt; &lt;destination&gt;</code>: Upload a file or directory from the host computer to the virtual device. If no destination path is specified, the file or directory is stored in <code>/sdcard/Downloads</code> by default.</li>
<li><code>pull &lt;source&gt; &lt;destination&gt;</code>: Copies a file or directory from the virtual device to the host computer. <strong>If a destination file already exists, it will be overwritten.</strong> Use <code>--all</code> option, to create a destination directory for each running virtual device.</li>
<li><code>install &lt;apk&gt;</code>: Installs an APK file on the virtual device.</li>
<li><code>flash &lt;archive&gt;</code>: Flash a <code>.zip</code> archive into the specified virtual device.</li>
<li><code>adbconnect</code>: Connects the specified virtual device using the ADB tool.</li>
<li><code>adbdisconnect</code>: Disconnects the specified virtual device from the ADB tool.</li>
</ul>
<div class="admonition example">
<p class="admonition-title">Example</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre id="__code_12"><span></span><nav class="md-code__nav"><button class="md-code__button" title="Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target="#__code_12 &gt; code" data-md-type="copy"></button></nav><code>./gmtool<span class="w"> </span>device<span class="w"> </span>logcatdump<span class="w"> </span>~/logcat-2021-12-02.txt
Writing<span class="w"> </span>logcat<span class="w"> </span><span class="k">for</span><span class="w"> </span>Samsung<span class="w"> </span>Galaxy<span class="w"> </span>S8_1<span class="w"> </span>into<span class="w"> </span>/home/user/logcat-2021-12-02.txt...
</code></pre></div>
</div>
<h2 id="error-messages">Error messages</h2>
<p>The table below explains error codes returned by GMTool:</p>
<div class="md-typeset__scrollwrap"><div class="md-typeset__table"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Code</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
